module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartierAffineLocal
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Spectrum.Prime.Module
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Noetherian

/-!
# From a principal stalk to a principal ideal sheaf

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme and `D ⊆ X` the closed subscheme cut out by a
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `ℐ`, presented as `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`.
[Stacks, Tag 0AG8] says that the two defining conditions on `D` can be checked one stalk at a
time: if `ℐ_x ⊆ 𝒪_{X,x}` is generated by one element for every `x ∈ D` then `D` is locally
principal, and if that generator can be taken to be a nonzerodivisor then `D` is an effective
Cartier divisor.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.isLocallyPrincipal_of_forall_stalk`: item (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0AG8].
* `Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_stalk`: item (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0AG8].

## Implementation notes

**The ring-theoretic core.**  On an affine open `U = Spec A` around `x` the stalk is the
localization `A_𝔭` of `A = Γ(X, U)` at the prime `𝔭` of `x`, and `ℐ_x` is the localized ideal.
Because `A` is Noetherian the ideal `I = ℐ(U)` is finitely generated, so each of its finitely
many generators is a multiple of the stalk generator up to a denominator and an equalizing
factor, none of which lie in `𝔭`.  `Stacks.Divisors.exists_notMem_forall_mul_mem_span` takes the
product of those finitely many elements: it returns a single `h ∉ 𝔭` and a `y ∈ I` with
`h * I ⊆ (y)`, and inverting `h` makes `I` principal on the generator `y`
(`Stacks.Divisors.map_eq_span_singleton_of_forall_mul_mem_span`).  Note that no power of `h` is
needed — one factor of `h` clears every element of `I` at once, because the equalizing factors
were absorbed into `h` before the product was taken.

**The nonzerodivisor half** is [Stacks, Tag 061L] for a single element and the module `A`:
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_notMem_annihilates` produces a `g ∉ 𝔭` annihilating the kernel of
multiplication by `y`, by the closedness of the support of that kernel as a finite module
(`Module.support_eq_zeroLocus`).  Taking the element in `Module.annihilator` outside `𝔭` gives
an annihilation on the nose rather than up to a power, which is why the conclusion of
`Stacks.Divisors.mem_nonZeroDivisors_map_of_annihilates` needs only divisibility and not a
localization-of-a-localization.  The two shrinkings are combined by inverting the single
element `h * g`, and both lemmas are therefore stated for an arbitrary multiple of the element
they are about.

**Transfer of the generator from the stalk.** The hypothesis names *some* generator of `ℐ_x`;
the proof produces its own, `y ∈ ℐ(U)`.  The two generate the same ideal of the stalk, and
`Stacks.Divisors.mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_span_singleton_eq` upgrades that to: a generator of a
principal ideal with one nonzerodivisor generator is itself a nonzerodivisor.  It needs no
locality — the two generators differ by a unit for the elementary reason that each divides the
other and the nonzerodivisor can be cancelled.

**The hypothesis is stated with an existential affine open**, as `∃ U, Ideal.map (germ U x) (ℐ U)`
is principal, rather than with the stalk ideal `ℐ_x` named abstractly — this presentation of a
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals records only the ideals `ℐ U` on affine opens, and has no
intrinsic stalk. For a fixed affine `U ∋ x` the germ image *is* `ℐ_x`, because the stalk is the
localization of `Γ(X, U)` at the prime of `x`, so the source's hypothesis implies this one for
every affine `U ∋ x` and in particular the existential; the theorems below are therefore at
least as strong as the source's. That identification is not itself formalized here, and nothing
below needs it: the proof consumes the germ image directly.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 061L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/061L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-! ### The ring-theoretic core -/

/-- If `h * z` lies in `(y)` for every generator `z` of an ideal, it does so for every element
of the ideal. -/
theorem forall_mul_mem_span_of_forall_mem {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (s : Set A) (h y : A)
    (hs : ∀ z ∈ s, h * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set A)) :
    ∀ z ∈ Ideal.span s, h * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set A) := by
  intro z hz
  induction hz using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem a ha => exact hs a ha
  | zero => simp
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [mul_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb
  | smul c a _ ha => rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_left_comm]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ ha

/-- One generator of the localized ideal clears a single generator of the ideal after
multiplication by an element outside the prime. -/
theorem exists_notMem_mul_mem_span {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A}
    {p : Ideal A} [p.IsPrime] {Ap : Type u} [CommRing Ap] [Algebra A Ap]
    [IsLocalization.AtPrime Ap p] {y : A}
    (hmap : I.map (algebraMap A Ap) = Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ap y})
    {z : A} (hz : z ∈ I) :
    ∃ t ∉ p, t * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set A) := by
  have hzm : algebraMap A Ap z ∈ Ideal.span ({algebraMap A Ap y} : Set Ap) := by
    rw [← hmap]; exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hz
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hzm
  obtain ⟨⟨a, v⟩, hav⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (M := p.primeCompl) c
  have key : algebraMap A Ap (z * (v : A)) = algebraMap A Ap (a * y) := by
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, ← hc, mul_comm c _, mul_assoc, hav]
    ring
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := (IsLocalization.eq_iff_exists p.primeCompl Ap).mp key
  refine ⟨(w : A) * (v : A), p.primeCompl.mul_mem w.2 v.2, ?_⟩
  exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨(w : A) * a, by linear_combination -hw⟩

/-- A finitely generated ideal whose localization at a prime `𝔭` is principal becomes principal
after multiplication by a single element outside `𝔭`: there are `h ∉ 𝔭` and `y ∈ I` with
`h * I ⊆ (y)`.  The generator `y` is produced inside `I` itself, and the localization of `I` at `𝔭`
is `(y)`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_forall_mul_mem_span
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A} (hI : I.FG)
    {p : Ideal A} [p.IsPrime] {Ap : Type u} [CommRing Ap] [Algebra A Ap]
    [IsLocalization.AtPrime Ap p]
    (hprin : (I.map (algebraMap A Ap)).IsPrincipal) :
    ∃ h ∉ p, ∃ y ∈ I, I.map (algebraMap A Ap) = Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ap y} ∧
      ∀ z ∈ I, h * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set A) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := hprin
  have hgm : g ∈ I.map (algebraMap A Ap) := by rw [hg]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self g
  obtain ⟨⟨⟨y, hyI⟩, u⟩, hyu⟩ := (IsLocalization.mem_map_algebraMap_iff p.primeCompl Ap).mp hgm
  have hmap : I.map (algebraMap A Ap) = Ideal.span {algebraMap A Ap y} := by
    rw [hg, ← hyu]
    exact (Ideal.span_singleton_mul_right_unit (IsLocalization.map_units Ap u) g).symm
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hI
  have H : ∀ z ∈ s, ∃ t, t ∉ p ∧ t * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set A) := fun z hz ↦
    exists_notMem_mul_mem_span (I := I) (p := p) (Ap := Ap) hmap
      (hs ▸ Ideal.subset_span (by exact_mod_cast hz))
  choose! T hT1 hT2 using H
  refine ⟨∏ z ∈ s, T z, p.primeCompl.prod_mem (fun c hc => hT1 c hc), y, hyI, hmap, ?_⟩
  rw [← hs]
  refine forall_mul_mem_span_of_forall_mem (s : Set A) _ y (fun z hz => ?_)
  have hzs : z ∈ s := by exact_mod_cast hz
  rw [← Finset.mul_prod_erase s T hzs, mul_right_comm]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (hT2 z hzs)

/-- If `h * I ⊆ (y)` with `y ∈ I`, then `I` is generated by `y` in any localization inverting a
multiple of `h`. -/
theorem map_eq_span_singleton_of_forall_mul_mem_span {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A}
    {h y t : A} (hyI : y ∈ I) (hmul : ∀ z ∈ I, h * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set A)) (hdvd : h ∣ t)
    (At : Type u) [CommRing At] [Algebra A At] [IsLocalization.Away t At] :
    I.map (algebraMap A At) = Ideal.span {algebraMap A At y} := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hdvd
  have hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap A At h) := by
    refine isUnit_of_mul_isUnit_left (y := algebraMap A At c) ?_
    rw [← map_mul, ← hc]
    exact IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit (S := At) t
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hunit.exists_left_inv
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp (hmul z hz)
    refine Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨b * algebraMap A At a, ?_⟩
    have h1 : algebraMap A At a * algebraMap A At y = algebraMap A At h * algebraMap A At z := by
      rw [← map_mul, ← map_mul, ha]
    linear_combination b * h1 + algebraMap A At z * hb
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hyI

/-- If `y` is a nonzerodivisor in the localization of a Noetherian ring at a prime `𝔭`, there is a
`g ∉ 𝔭` annihilating everything that `y` annihilates. -/
theorem exists_notMem_annihilates
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {p : Ideal A} [p.IsPrime]
    {Ap : Type u} [CommRing Ap] [Algebra A Ap] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Ap p]
    {y : A} (hy : algebraMap A Ap y ∈ nonZeroDivisors Ap) :
    ∃ g ∉ p, ∀ a : A, y * a = 0 → g * a = 0 := by
  classical
  set K := LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.mulLeft A y) with hK
  have hfin : Module.Finite A ↥K := Module.Finite.iff_fg.mpr (IsNoetherian.noetherian K)
  have hsub : Subsingleton (LocalizedModule p.primeCompl ↥K) := by
    rw [LocalizedModule.subsingleton_iff]
    intro m
    have hm : y * (m : A) = 0 := LinearMap.mem_ker.mp m.2
    have hz : algebraMap A Ap (m : A) = 0 := by
      refine (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff.mp hy).1 _ ?_
      rw [← map_mul, hm, map_zero]
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff p.primeCompl Ap (m : A)).mp hz
    exact ⟨r, r.2, by ext; simpa using hr⟩
  have hnot : (⟨p, ‹p.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum A) ∉ Module.support A ↥K := by
    rw [Module.mem_support_iff]
    exact fun hc => (not_nontrivial_iff_subsingleton.mpr hsub) hc
  rw [Module.support_eq_zeroLocus, PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus] at hnot
  obtain ⟨g, hgann, hgp⟩ := Set.not_subset.mp hnot
  refine ⟨g, hgp, fun a ha => ?_⟩
  have h2 : g • (⟨a, LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr (by simpa using ha)⟩ : ↥K) = 0 :=
    Module.mem_annihilator.mp hgann _
  simpa using congrArg Subtype.val h2

/-- If `g` annihilates everything `y` annihilates, then `y` is a nonzerodivisor in any
localization inverting a multiple of `g`. -/
theorem mem_nonZeroDivisors_map_of_annihilates
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {y g t : A}
    (hg : ∀ a : A, y * a = 0 → g * a = 0) (hdvd : g ∣ t)
    (At : Type u) [CommRing At] [Algebra A At] [IsLocalization.Away t At] :
    algebraMap A At y ∈ nonZeroDivisors At := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hdvd
  have hgen : ∀ b : A, g * b = 0 → t * b = 0 := fun b hb ↦ by
    rw [hc]
    linear_combination c * hb
  have main : ∀ ξ : At, algebraMap A At y * ξ = 0 → ξ = 0 := by
    intro ξ h0
    obtain ⟨⟨a, m⟩, ham⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (M := Submonoid.powers t) ξ
    have hya : algebraMap A At (y * a) = 0 := by
      rw [map_mul, ← ham, ← mul_assoc, h0, zero_mul]
    obtain ⟨m', hm'⟩ :=
      (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff (Submonoid.powers t) At (y * a)).mp hya
    have h1 : y * ((m' : A) * a) = 0 := by linear_combination hm'
    have h3 : (t * (m' : A)) * a = 0 := by
      rw [mul_assoc]; exact hgen _ (hg _ h1)
    have h4 : algebraMap A At a = 0 :=
      (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff (Submonoid.powers t) At a).mpr
        ⟨⟨t * (m' : A), Submonoid.mul_mem _ (Submonoid.mem_powers t) m'.2⟩, h3⟩
    have h5 : ξ * algebraMap A At (m : A) = 0 := by rw [ham, h4]
    exact (IsUnit.mul_left_eq_zero (IsLocalization.map_units At m)).mp h5
  exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mpr main

/-- A generator of a principal ideal that has one nonzerodivisor generator is itself a
nonzerodivisor: the nonzerodivisor generator is a multiple of it, so anything it kills is
killed by the nonzerodivisor too. -/
theorem mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_span_singleton_eq {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {a b : A}
    (hab : Ideal.span ({a} : Set A) = Ideal.span ({b} : Set A))
    (hb : b ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) : a ∈ nonZeroDivisors A := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp (hab.symm ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self b)
  refine mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mpr fun x hx => ?_
  exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mp hb x (by linear_combination d * hx - x * hd)

/-! ### The two items of Tag 0AG8 -/

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- A section outside the prime of `x` in an affine open `U` does not vanish at `x`. -/
private theorem mem_basicOpen_of_notMem_primeIdealOf (U : X.affineOpens) {x : X}
    (hxU : x ∈ (U : Set X)) {h : Γ(X, U.1)}
    (hh : h ∉ (U.2.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)).asIdeal) : x ∈ X.basicOpen h := by
  let _ := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)
  have _ := U.2.isLocalization_stalk (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)
  exact (X.mem_basicOpen h x hxU).mpr ((IsLocalization.AtPrime.isUnit_to_map_iff
    (X.presheaf.stalk x) (U.2.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)).asIdeal h).mpr hh)

/-- The ring of sections on `affineBasicOpen t` is the localization of `Γ(X, U)` away from `t`. -/
private theorem isLocalization_away_affineBasicOpen (U : X.affineOpens) (t : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    letI : Algebra Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, (X.affineBasicOpen t).1) :=
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.affineBasicOpen_le t)).op).hom.toAlgebra
    IsLocalization.Away t Γ(X, (X.affineBasicOpen t).1) :=
  U.2.isLocalization_of_eq_basicOpen t (homOfLE (X.affineBasicOpen_le t)) rfl

/-- On an affine open `U` around `x`, a principal stalk ideal yields an `h ∈ Γ(X, U)` not
vanishing at `x` and a `y ∈ ℐ(U)` with `h * ℐ(U) ⊆ (y)`, with `y` generating `ℐ_x`. -/
theorem exists_basicOpen_forall_mul_mem_span [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    {x : X} (U : X.affineOpens) (hxU : x ∈ (U : Set X))
    (hprin : (Ideal.map (X.presheaf.germ U.1 x hxU).hom (I.ideal U)).IsPrincipal) :
    ∃ h : Γ(X, U.1), x ∈ X.basicOpen h ∧ ∃ y ∈ I.ideal U,
      Ideal.map (X.presheaf.germ U.1 x hxU).hom (I.ideal U)
          = Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U.1 x hxU).hom y} ∧
        ∀ z ∈ I.ideal U, h * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set Γ(X, U.1)) := by
  let _ := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)
  have _ := U.2.isLocalization_stalk (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)
  have _ : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
  obtain ⟨h, hhp, y, hyI, hmap, hmul⟩ :=
    exists_notMem_forall_mul_mem_span (A := Γ(X, U.1)) (Ap := X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (p := (U.2.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)).asIdeal) (IsNoetherian.noetherian _) hprin
  exact ⟨h, mem_basicOpen_of_notMem_primeIdealOf U hxU hhp, y, hyI, hmap, hmul⟩

/-- Inverting a multiple of `h` makes `ℐ` principal on `y`. -/
theorem ideal_affineBasicOpen_eq_span (U : X.affineOpens) {h y t : Γ(X, U.1)}
    (hyI : y ∈ I.ideal U)
    (hmul : ∀ z ∈ I.ideal U, h * z ∈ Ideal.span ({y} : Set Γ(X, U.1))) (hdvd : h ∣ t) :
    I.ideal (X.affineBasicOpen t)
      = Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.affineBasicOpen_le t)).op).hom y} := by
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, (X.affineBasicOpen t).1) :=
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.affineBasicOpen_le t)).op).hom.toAlgebra
  have _ := isLocalization_away_affineBasicOpen U t
  rw [← I.map_ideal (X.affineBasicOpen_le t)]
  exact map_eq_span_singleton_of_forall_mul_mem_span hyI hmul hdvd _

/-- If the stalk of the ideal sheaf at every point of the closed subscheme can be generated by one
element, the subscheme is locally principal. -/
@[stacks 0AG8 "(1)"]
theorem isLocallyPrincipal_of_forall_stalk [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (hst : ∀ x ∈ I.supportSet, ∃ (U : X.affineOpens) (hxU : x ∈ (U : Set X)),
      (Ideal.map (X.presheaf.germ U.1 x hxU).hom (I.ideal U)).IsPrincipal) :
    IsLocallyPrincipal I := by
  intro x
  by_cases hx : x ∈ I.supportSet
  · obtain ⟨U, hxU, hprin⟩ := hst x hx
    obtain ⟨h, hxh, y, hyI, -, hmul⟩ :=
      exists_basicOpen_forall_mul_mem_span I U hxU hprin
    exact ⟨X.affineBasicOpen h, hxh, _, ideal_affineBasicOpen_eq_span I U hyI hmul dvd_rfl⟩
  · obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, f, -, hgen⟩ :=
      exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_notMem_support I x hx
    exact ⟨⟨U, hU⟩, hxU, f, hgen⟩

/-- If the stalk of the ideal sheaf at every point of the closed subscheme can be generated by a
single nonzerodivisor, the subscheme is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
@[stacks 0AG8 "(2)"]
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_stalk [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (hst : ∀ x ∈ I.supportSet, ∃ (U : X.affineOpens) (hxU : x ∈ (U : Set X)),
      ∃ ξ ∈ nonZeroDivisors (X.presheaf.stalk x),
        Ideal.map (X.presheaf.germ U.1 x hxU).hom (I.ideal U) = Ideal.span {ξ}) :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I := by
  refine isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen I fun x => ?_
  by_cases hx : x ∈ I.supportSet
  · obtain ⟨U, hxU, ξ, hξ, hgen⟩ := hst x hx
    let _ := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)
    have _ := U.2.isLocalization_stalk (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)
    have _ : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
    obtain ⟨h, hxh, y, hyI, hmap, hmul⟩ :=
      exists_basicOpen_forall_mul_mem_span I U hxU ⟨ξ, hgen⟩
    have hynzd : (X.presheaf.germ U.1 x hxU).hom y ∈ nonZeroDivisors (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_span_singleton_eq (hmap.symm.trans hgen) hξ
    obtain ⟨g, hgp, hgann⟩ :=
      exists_notMem_annihilates (A := Γ(X, U.1)) (Ap := X.presheaf.stalk x)
        (p := (U.2.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxU⟩ : U.1)).asIdeal) hynzd
    have hxg := mem_basicOpen_of_notMem_primeIdealOf U hxU hgp
    refine ⟨(X.affineBasicOpen (h * g)).1, (X.affineBasicOpen (h * g)).2, ?_, _, ?_,
      ideal_affineBasicOpen_eq_span I U hyI hmul (dvd_mul_right h g)⟩
    · exact show x ∈ X.basicOpen (h * g) by rw [X.basicOpen_mul]; exact ⟨hxh, hxg⟩
    · let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U.1) Γ(X, (X.affineBasicOpen (h * g)).1) :=
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.affineBasicOpen_le (h * g))).op).hom.toAlgebra
      have _ := isLocalization_away_affineBasicOpen U (h * g)
      exact isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mpr
        (mem_nonZeroDivisors_map_of_annihilates hgann (dvd_mul_left g h) _)
  · exact exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_notMem_support I x hx

end Stacks.Divisors

end
